From: OpenBMC Orange Pi Zero 2 integration
Subject: [PATCH] Kvm: keep pointer in the captured framebuffer coordinate space

The CH32V307 presents an absolute-coordinate USB HID pointer. Keep noVNC's
framebuffer as the single pointer coordinate source: scale the rendered canvas
without resizing the remote session, disable viewport panning, and let noVNC
convert browser canvas coordinates back to framebuffer coordinates before it
sends each RFB pointer event.

With this contract, CSS/display scaling does not change the logical pointer
position and obmc-ikvm can map the negotiated capture frame directly to the
HID range 0..0x7fff.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific external HID integration]

diff --git a/src/views/Operations/Kvm/KvmConsole.vue b/src/views/Operations/Kvm/KvmConsole.vue
index 438ee9a..f630f5e 100644
--- a/src/views/Operations/Kvm/KvmConsole.vue
+++ b/src/views/Operations/Kvm/KvmConsole.vue
@@ -146,8 +146,15 @@ export default {
         { wsProtocols: [token] },
       );
 
+      // Keep the negotiated video framebuffer as the one absolute coordinate
+      // space. noVNC divides canvas coordinates by its viewport scale before
+      // sending RFB pointer events, so the CH32V307 HID cursor remains aligned
+      // at every browser size and captured-video resolution.
       this.rfb.scaleViewport = true;
-      this.rfb.clipViewport = true;
+      this.rfb.clipViewport = false;
+      this.rfb.dragViewport = false;
+      this.rfb.resizeSession = false;
+      this.rfb.viewOnly = false;
       const that = this;
 
       this.resizeKvmWindow = throttle(() => {
